{
  "notes": [
    "tensorcore_slowdown_ms = how much longer the TensorCore itself was busy in the combined run than in the workload-alone run; edge_cost_ms is the remainder of the marginal cost (launch and drain).",
    "trace_overlap is the fraction of SparseCore busy time that fell inside TensorCore busy time.  It can be 1.0 while hidden is near 0.0: running concurrently is not the same as running for free.",
    "xla_over_sparsecore > 1 means the SparseCore kernel is the cheaper way to gather alongside this workload."
  ],
  "note": "hidden = 1 - (T_both - T_workload) / T_gather_alone.  1.0 means the gather was fully overlapped and cost nothing; 0.0 means it was fully serialized; negative means it contended with the workload and cost more than running it alone.",
